WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.077
QuickStart 1 · Illumina
Open browser setup after downloading and verifying the reads. This recording uses synthetic file listings and checks.

2
00:00:05.077 --> 00:00:11.832
QuickStart 1 · Illumina · preservation
Choose preservation from specimen records. Fresh is selected only as demonstration metadata here.

3
00:00:11.832 --> 00:00:26.337
QuickStart 1 · Illumina · discover inputs
Review the prefilled FASTQ folder, then choose Discover samples. Each Illumina read pair stays together.

4
00:00:26.337 --> 00:00:33.812
QuickStart 1 · Illumina · sample groups
Assign the example sample to Cancer. Use the type dropdown; you can also drag cards between groups.

5
00:00:33.812 --> 00:00:42.215
QuickStart 1 · Illumina · CNA settings
Keep Copy-number analysis and set a CPU budget. This Illumina example uses QDNAseq with 100 kb bins.

6
00:00:42.215 --> 00:00:48.665
QuickStart 1 · Illumina · tools and reference
Choose the backend you installed. Keep prepared hg38 download; real downloads begin only when you start analysis.

7
00:00:48.665 --> 00:00:55.398
QuickStart 1 · Illumina · separate project
Confirm a distinct project folder. Keep optional short-variant analysis off for this CNA QuickStart.

8
00:00:55.398 --> 00:01:02.156
QuickStart 1 · Illumina · save and review
Save configuration and check. Resolve any errors before Run analysis. These displayed checks are simulated.

9
00:01:02.156 --> 00:01:08.792
QuickStart 1 · Illumina · ready for your run
In a real project, choose Run analysis after checks pass and keep its terminal open. This demo stops here; no analysis was run.
